---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Terms of Service" description={`Terms for using ${site.domain} and engaging ${site.name} for services.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-site max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="h2 mt-3">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] text-ink-soft">Effective {site.termsEffective}</p>

      <div class="prose-site mt-8 text-ink-soft [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:mb-4 [&_li]:mb-1">
        <p>These terms cover your use of {site.domain} (the "Site") and, at a high level, how {site.legalName} ("{site.name}," "I," "we") works with clients. Specific engagements are governed by a written scope or agreement, which controls if it conflicts with anything here.</p>

        <h2>Using the Site</h2>
        <p>The Site is provided for information and to request services. Don't use it to send spam, scrape content, probe for vulnerabilities, or submit false information. Content on the Site belongs to {site.legalName} unless noted; you can share links to it freely.</p>

        <h2>How engagements work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Audit.</strong> A fixed-fee engagement ({site.auditPrice} unless quoted otherwise), typically {site.auditDuration}, that ends in a written, prioritized plan. Payment is due before work starts unless the scope says otherwise.</li>
          <li><strong>Build.</strong> Fixed-scope work quoted from the audit. Changes to scope are quoted separately before they're done.</li>
          <li><strong>Operate.</strong> An optional monthly retainer, billed in advance, cancellable with 30 days' notice by either side.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What you're responsible for</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Providing access to the systems and data needed for the work, and having the right to grant that access.</li>
          <li>Reviewing deliverables and telling us promptly if something's off.</li>
          <li>Decisions about your business. Deliverables are recommendations and tools; you decide what to act on.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>No guarantee of results</h2>
        <p>Case studies and figures on the Site describe past work for specific clients. They are not a promise that your results will match. Revenue, ad performance, and email outcomes depend on many things outside our control.</p>

        <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>We keep client data and business information confidential and use it only to do the work. We don't name clients publicly without permission.</p>

        <h2>Ownership</h2>
        <p>Once paid for, deliverables built specifically for you (reports, workflows, spreadsheets, configurations) are yours. We keep the right to reuse general know-how, methods, and non-client-specific templates.</p>

        <h2>Third-party tools</h2>
        <p>Work often runs on platforms you own accounts with (Shopify, email platforms, Zapier, n8n, Google, Meta, and others). Their terms and pricing apply to you directly. We aren't responsible for their outages, changes, or fees.</p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>To the extent permitted by law, {site.legalName}'s total liability for any claim related to the Site or services is limited to the fees you paid for the specific engagement in question. We aren't liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, including lost profits.</p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Arizona. Disputes will be handled in the state or federal courts located in Maricopa County, Arizona.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms; the effective date at the top will change when we do. Continued use of the Site after a change means you accept it.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>{site.legalName}<br />{site.mailingAddress}<br /><a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="link">{site.contactEmail}</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
